# Project 02 – Static Website on Amazon S3 with Terraform

Hosts a static website on Amazon S3. Every resource is created with Terraform: the bucket, website hosting, public-read policy and the HTML files.

## Architecture
```
Lab VM (terraform apply) ──creates──► S3 bucket (us-east-2)
                                       ├─ Website hosting (index.html / error.html)
                                       ├─ Block Public Access: off (bucket level)
                                       ├─ Bucket policy: Allow s3:GetObject to *
                                       └─ Objects: index.html, error.html
Browser ──HTTP GET──► S3 website endpoint
```

## Files
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `providers.tf` | AWS (~> 5.0) and random (~> 3.0) providers, region from variable |
| `variables.tf` | `region` (us-east-2), `bucket_prefix` |
| `main.tf` | Bucket, website config, public access block, bucket policy, HTML uploads |
| `outputs.tf` | `bucket_name`, `website_url` |
| `website/index.html` | Home page |
| `website/error.html` | Custom 404 page |

## Resources created
- `random_id` – unique suffix, because bucket names are global
- `aws_s3_bucket` – the bucket (`force_destroy = true` for easy cleanup)
- `aws_s3_bucket_website_configuration` – index and error documents
- `aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block` – allows a public policy on this bucket
- `aws_s3_bucket_policy` – public read-only (`s3:GetObject`) on all objects
- `aws_s3_object` x2 – uploads HTML with `content_type = text/html`

## How to deploy
```bash
cd Project-02
terraform init
terraform plan
terraform apply -auto-approve
terraform output -raw website_url
```

## Testing
```bash
curl $(terraform output -raw website_url)          # returns index.html
curl -i $(terraform output -raw website_url)/abc   # returns 404 + error.html
```

## Output
**Website URL:** http://raunak-capstone-p2-e26d0ed0.s3-website.us-east-2.amazonaws.com

![Website](Screenshot%202026-11-20%20011215.png)

## Issues faced
| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| URL opened as a Google search | Copied with quotes; used `terraform output -raw` |
| `git push` rejected (fetch first) | `git pull --rebase origin main`, then push |

## Notes
- S3 website endpoints are **HTTP only**. That's why the browser shows "Not Secure". HTTPS needs CloudFront + ACM.
- The policy allows read only: no list, upload or delete.

## Cleanup
```bash
terraform destroy -auto-approve
```
